From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] cocoa: the guest's IOSurface buffer as the layer's contents (prototype)

What: with OMACVM_GL_PRESENT_DIRECT=1 and a scanout buffer that virgl made
as an IOSurface (virgl-scanout-iosurface.patch, OMACVM_SCANOUT_IOSURFACE=1),
a frame goes on the layer as that buffer: no draw into the present's
surfaces. It waits for the guest's GPU work as a drawn frame waits for the
draw (a fence after the guest's flush) and takes the vsync queue like any
frame. Frames that must be drawn (the boot logo, extra brightness, 10-bit,
part of the buffer, a size the surfaces do not have yet, upside down, the
buffer shown last flushed again, the tiled present) are drawn from the
IOSurface as a RECTANGLE texture; the partial present then draws them in
full. The buffer is tagged sRGB as the present's surfaces are. DisplayGLTexture
carries the IOSurface (virtio-gpu-virgl.c asks virgl for it).
qemu.log every 5 s: "cocoa: present-direct: direct N, <reason> M ...".
Test hook OMACVM_TEST_PACE_CHECK=1 (with pace2.html: tests/graphics/pacing's
page with a second counter strip at the bottom): each whole frame's
counters are read from its surface as it goes up (plain 8-bit surfaces): top
and bottom must agree, the frame before must still hold its own counter (not
written while shown), and the steps between frames are counted; marker
flips are logged for key latency.
Why: the present's draw is 0.45 ms of GPU per frame at 5K, 120 frames a
second (54 ms/s); WindowServer shows a full-screen IOSurface without
compositing either way.
Limits: no extra brightness for such buffers (drawn without the gain);
8-bit SDR only.
TODO(revert: prototype on branch present-direct-surface, not for main as it is).
Upstream: not sent (OmacVM's IOSurface present).
Tests: VM A/B in docs/experiments/display-path.md.
Applies after omacvm-cocoa-no-app-nap.patch, with virgl-scanout-iosurface.patch.
